    ],
    "text": "STATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      292.27,
      455.55,
      330.38
    ],
    "text": "Clause 2: This clause amends section 3(1) of Maternity Benefits Ordinance (hereinafterreferred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) and the legal effect of the section as amended is toprovide provisions for a woman worker for the period for which maternity benefits shall bepaid.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      340.63,
      455.54,
      369.14
    ],
    "text": "Clause 3: This clause amends section 5 of the principal enactment and the legal effect ofthe section as amended is to provide provisions for the payment of maternity benefits for thewoman worker at the prescribed rate.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      379.39,
      455.54,
      407.78
    ],
    "text": "Clause 4: This clause amends section 6 of the principal enactment and the legal effect ofthe section as amended is to provide provisions for woman worker not to claim benefits inrespect of same confinement from more than one employer.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      418.15,
      455.54,
      446.66
    ],
    "text": "Clause 5: This clause amends section 7 of the principal enactment and the legal effect ofthe section as amended is to provide for a woman worker to inform her employer of the dayof the confinement for the purpose of calculating the leave of the confinement.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      456.91,
      455.54,
      495.14
    ],
    "text": "Clause 6: This clause amends section 8 of the principal enactment and the legal effect ofthe section as amended is to inform the employer of any woman worker whether or not herconfinement resulted in the issue of live child or not in order to ascertain the period for thepayment of maternity benefits.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      505.39,
      455.55,
      533.78
    ],
    "text": "Clause 7: This clause amends section 11 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof the section as amended is to delete the words \u201calternative maternity benefits\u201d from thesection 11 of the principal enactment.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      544.15,
      455.5,
      562.94
    ],
    "text": "Clause 8: This clause amends section 15 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof the section as amended is to repeal paragraph (f) of subsection (2) of section 15.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
