    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      268.61,
      401.9,
      292.91
    ],
    "text": "BE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      307.61,
      401.88,
      331.91
    ],
    "text": "1.This Act may be cited as the Maternity Benefits(Amendment) Act, No. of 2018.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      346.61,
      401.92,
      396.95
    ],
    "text": "2.Section 3 of the Maternity Benefits Ordinance(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is herebyamended by the repealed of subsection (1) of that sectionand substitution therefor, of the following subsection:\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      186.81,
      411.65,
      401.89,
      448.91
    ],
    "text": "\u201c(1) The period for which any woman worker shallbe entitled to the payment of maternity benefits shallbe\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      213.57,
      463.61,
      401.88,
      526.91
    ],
    "text": "(a)twelve weeks, that is to say two weeks upto and including the day of herconfinement and ten weeks immediatelyfollowing that day, if the confinementresults in the issue of a live child; and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      213.57,
      541.61,
      401.88,
      604.91
    ],
    "text": "(b)six weeks, that is to say two weeks up toand including the day of her confinementand four weeks immediately followingthat day, if the confinement does not resultin the issue of a live child:",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      185.85,
      619.61,
      401.88,
      669.95
    ],
    "text": "Provided however, that where such woman workerhas worked in her employment for any number of daysduring the aforesaid period of two weeks referred to inparagraphs (a) and (b) she shall be entitled to the",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      407.85,
      348.91,
      451.29,
      386.78
    ],
